WEBVTT

00:07.710 --> 00:09.550
Once I turn that corner,

00:09.550 --> 00:11.860
I'll see the student council
office to the left.

00:12.450 --> 00:15.130
Today, I will knock on that door.

00:15.770 --> 00:17.860
It doesn't seem like a big deal now, but...

00:36.190 --> 00:39.620
I served as student council
president in my school days.

00:40.570 --> 00:44.900
Well, there were only 26 students
in my entire middle school.

00:44.900 --> 00:53.310
Still, my young mind was always looking
for ideas to improve student life.

00:54.210 --> 00:57.870
I think that experience helps me to this day.

00:58.800 --> 01:04.260
Yeah, this may be one
small step for a girl...

01:04.760 --> 01:05.880
However...

01:05.880 --> 01:09.210
It's one giant leap for Japanese society!

01:09.990 --> 01:12.670
Let's go, Aldrin-kun, Collins-ku—

01:12.670 --> 01:14.760
I mean, Shima-kun, Yuzuki-chan!

01:14.760 --> 01:15.580
Huh?

01:15.930 --> 01:16.730
Oh.

01:23.110 --> 01:24.430
Someone beat me to it.

02:56.810 --> 02:58.020
That's Kurume-san.

02:58.020 --> 03:00.650
Oh, the one who sits diagonally behind you?

03:00.650 --> 03:05.610
I wonder if she wants to
join the student council, too.

03:05.610 --> 03:07.160
Why don't you ask her?

03:07.760 --> 03:11.590
What do I do?
Am I gonna be a bother?

03:11.590 --> 03:15.170
This does feel like a place that would
attract serious, diligent people,

03:15.540 --> 03:19.690
but can you join just by asking?

03:22.840 --> 03:24.470
Trendy gals were never an option,

03:24.470 --> 03:29.020
and I'll never be friends with the girls
flocking to some "stud," either.

03:29.020 --> 03:31.760
While I was busy whittling down my options,

03:31.760 --> 03:34.270
I was left completely
hung out to dry in class.

03:34.740 --> 03:37.620
I need to find some sort of
community for myself, and fast!

03:38.110 --> 03:39.680
Aren't you gonna go in?

03:42.660 --> 03:44.280
Sorry if I startled you!

03:45.090 --> 03:47.280
I-Iwakura Mitsumi!

03:47.660 --> 03:49.670
Despite her model-student appearance,

03:49.670 --> 03:52.380
she ran into our teacher on our
first day and puked all over her.

03:52.380 --> 03:55.200
An enigma who's even rumored
to be the Secret Boss of our school.

03:55.200 --> 03:57.510
You're Kurume-san, right?

03:57.510 --> 03:58.590
Huh...

03:58.590 --> 03:59.230
Ack!

03:59.230 --> 04:01.800
The student council office's
all the way out here?

04:02.150 --> 04:04.130
Did you join it in middle school, too?

04:04.130 --> 04:05.290
Of course!

04:05.290 --> 04:08.000
I was the leader of the
student body, all 26 of us!

04:08.000 --> 04:09.000
Wow.

04:09.000 --> 04:11.140
And the himbo, Shima Sousuke!

04:11.520 --> 04:13.120
Why are they with her?

04:13.120 --> 04:14.520
Is she really...

04:14.520 --> 04:15.640
the Secret Boss?!

04:15.640 --> 04:18.630
Are you interested in the
student council, Kurume-san?

04:19.450 --> 04:20.820
K-Kinda.

04:20.820 --> 04:23.320
Huh...

04:23.320 --> 04:26.570
Huh? Did I just make a big mistake?

04:27.150 --> 04:28.940
Yeah!

04:28.940 --> 04:31.330
I'm glad to have a classmate with me!

04:32.660 --> 04:34.020
She's being shy, isn't she?

04:34.020 --> 04:35.290
Yeah, probably.

04:37.070 --> 04:39.920
Because I was born to lead, obviously!

04:39.920 --> 04:43.630
D-Don't misunderstand! I don't
want to be president or anything!

04:43.630 --> 04:45.430
Oh, okay.

04:47.810 --> 04:50.650
I'm off. Good luck, Mitsumi.

04:50.650 --> 04:52.560
Aren't you gonna check it out?

04:52.560 --> 04:55.070
Nah, I'm not at all interested.

04:56.060 --> 04:56.900
Bye.

04:56.900 --> 04:58.970
See you!

04:58.970 --> 05:00.770
She's looking down on me!

05:01.680 --> 05:03.400
Okay, time to get this back on track.

05:03.770 --> 05:05.290
Let's go in!

05:05.290 --> 05:06.940
Yeah!

05:08.070 --> 05:09.260
Huh?

05:09.260 --> 05:12.200
The student government
doesn't recruit members.

05:17.050 --> 05:19.940
Thank you. Sorry for bothering you.

05:19.940 --> 05:22.880
Well, have some tea before you go.

05:23.510 --> 05:27.050
It makes me happy that you're interested.

05:27.050 --> 05:31.080
Oh, I'm Yamamoto, a third-year.
I'm the student council president.

05:31.080 --> 05:33.310
I'm Takamine, a second-year. I'm a treasurer.

05:33.310 --> 05:36.380
The government has tenure,
so you can't join yet.

05:36.380 --> 05:39.270
But you can apply to join our support team.

05:40.310 --> 05:42.610
It's called the Tsubame Society.

05:42.610 --> 05:45.570
You'll work with us on events
such as the school festival.

05:45.960 --> 05:48.230
People who want to join
the student government

05:48.230 --> 05:52.200
or don't mind just helping out
with events join it.

05:52.630 --> 05:54.500
Any questions?

05:54.950 --> 05:59.080
How do you balance student
government work with your studies?

05:59.080 --> 06:00.620
Oh, right.

06:00.620 --> 06:02.210
How do you handle it, Takamine-san?

06:02.670 --> 06:03.960
Ahem.

06:03.960 --> 06:08.180
Well, I'd be lying if I said there
weren't any time constraints.

06:08.180 --> 06:11.460
Sometimes, we stay back late
preparing for meetings and things.

06:11.460 --> 06:12.590
That bad?

06:13.100 --> 06:15.930
This is... concerning.

06:16.800 --> 06:20.680
I asked my family to send me to Tokyo
so I could prep for and apply to Tokyo U.

06:20.680 --> 06:25.070
It'd suck if I failed to get in because
I was too busy with the student council.

06:25.830 --> 06:26.830
But...

06:28.370 --> 06:32.260
I don't believe it's bad enough
to affect one's grades.

06:32.750 --> 06:37.160
Making the most of your time
is what matters, don't you think?

06:38.330 --> 06:39.630
So cool!

06:40.450 --> 06:43.530
But how much time you spend matters, too!

06:43.530 --> 06:45.170
Oh, right, take a look.

06:45.170 --> 06:49.500
This is my planner. I hope it helps.

06:49.930 --> 06:52.570
I break my schedule down to the minute.

06:52.570 --> 06:55.810
That makes every task smaller, each one
giving you a sense of accomplishment,

06:55.810 --> 06:57.080
so I recommend it.

06:59.190 --> 07:01.810
I was trying to take the easy way out.

07:02.940 --> 07:05.140
I'll take note of that, Senpai!

07:07.450 --> 07:08.830
Thank you for your time!

07:08.830 --> 07:10.720
No problem. Take care.

07:11.450 --> 07:13.840
Well, I'll be leaving now.

07:13.840 --> 07:15.950
Okay, see you.

07:17.200 --> 07:18.380
Kurume-san...

07:19.880 --> 07:22.000
I wonder if she'll join the Tsubame Society.

07:22.000 --> 07:23.710
I want to ask her a bunch of things.

07:24.210 --> 07:29.900
Thinking back, I only ever exchanged contact
IDs because someone else did the asking.

07:31.420 --> 07:35.080
If I leave everything to luck,
I'll never be on <i>Atsuatsu Tairiku.</i>

07:35.080 --> 07:37.350
Last week's episode was pretty cool.

07:38.650 --> 07:40.390
Man, that was so scary!

07:40.390 --> 07:42.350
Maybe I'll check out
the literature club tomorrow.

07:42.350 --> 07:43.850
Kurume-san!

07:48.170 --> 07:49.610
You walk fast.

07:52.070 --> 07:54.710
Do you have some time today?

08:01.770 --> 08:05.380
Drinking one of these has been
on my bucket list forever!

08:06.080 --> 08:10.380
I'd intended never to drink
such a goofy drink.

08:10.380 --> 08:14.550
Bucket list? There's gotta be at least
one Starmax in Ishikawa, too.

08:14.550 --> 08:17.570
There is. But it's three hours away by bus.

08:17.570 --> 08:19.840
Can I take off this lid?

08:20.240 --> 08:21.890
What is going on here?

08:22.380 --> 08:26.370
Anyway, I'm surprised she wanted
to go to a Starmax.

08:26.370 --> 08:29.530
This looks pretty filling to me.

08:30.790 --> 08:33.180
Do you like sweet things, Kurume-san?

08:33.220 --> 08:34.080
I guess.

08:34.080 --> 08:36.830
My aunt tells me this one's really good.

08:36.830 --> 08:39.480
It's so hard to resist something
"limited," isn't it?

08:39.480 --> 08:40.910
Sure is.

08:41.750 --> 08:45.100
Why did I order the same thing, too?

08:45.100 --> 08:47.670
I gave in to peer pressure!

08:48.110 --> 08:49.120
To battle.

09:03.520 --> 09:05.790
It's so good!

09:06.730 --> 09:09.050
So rich and chewy!

09:09.050 --> 09:10.360
Glad you like it.

09:10.360 --> 09:12.700
I've never had boba before.

09:12.700 --> 09:15.120
Don't convenience stores in Ishikawa have it?

09:15.120 --> 09:16.180
Maybe!

09:20.220 --> 09:22.440
This is better than I expected.

09:27.260 --> 09:28.500
Dammit!

09:29.210 --> 09:31.510
Are you two joining the Tsubame Society?

09:31.510 --> 09:33.240
I'm going to join.

09:33.240 --> 09:35.490
I need to think about it.

09:35.490 --> 09:38.140
I only went with Mitsumi-chan
because I was bored.

09:38.140 --> 09:42.400
Really? But you told Kanechika-senpai...

09:42.400 --> 09:45.100
Shima-kun! Join me in the drama club!

09:45.100 --> 09:48.000
Sorry, I've decided to join
the student council.

09:48.000 --> 09:49.540
Let's go, Mitsumi-chan.

09:49.940 --> 09:52.650
Well, that guy just doesn't
take no for an answer.

09:52.650 --> 09:54.950
It's not good to lie like that.

09:54.950 --> 09:56.420
Sorry about that.

09:57.700 --> 09:59.020
What's up?

09:59.020 --> 10:01.120
Nothing. It's just surprising.

10:01.120 --> 10:02.020
What is?

10:02.020 --> 10:06.230
I mean, you two get along
even though you're so different.

10:06.230 --> 10:08.790
I was wondering how you do it.

10:09.700 --> 10:10.590
"How"?

10:10.590 --> 10:14.300
Well, it's not like everyone with
similar tastes gets along, either.

10:14.660 --> 10:16.890
It's probably the little things that matter.

10:16.890 --> 10:19.800
Like how food tastes better
when you eat with that person.

10:27.480 --> 10:28.890
K... Kurume-san.

10:29.500 --> 10:31.150
Do you wanna exchange IDs?

10:32.820 --> 10:33.730
Sure.

10:37.610 --> 10:39.200
"Thank you."

10:43.370 --> 10:46.060
Huh? I got a message from Yuzuki-chan.

10:47.580 --> 10:50.190
"How'd it go with the student council?"

10:50.190 --> 10:51.940
Oh, she's worried about you!

10:51.940 --> 10:54.330
I know! Let's send her a picture!

10:54.330 --> 10:56.630
Like, "We're at Starmax!"

10:58.660 --> 10:59.760
Huh? Wha?

10:59.760 --> 11:02.340
Oh, should I point it this way?

11:02.340 --> 11:04.280
Uh, Mitsumi-chan, that's...

11:04.280 --> 11:06.010
Hmm? Squeeze in!

11:07.960 --> 11:09.520
It's all blurry!

11:09.520 --> 11:11.110
Wh-Wh-Why?!

11:11.640 --> 11:13.210
Let's just send her this!

11:13.210 --> 11:16.330
Wait, don't! A-Ahh!

11:21.610 --> 11:23.320
She's super sad about it!

11:23.320 --> 11:25.490
Is this what Murashige-san's really like?

11:25.950 --> 11:31.040
Wait, wait, Shima-kun! I need to get
a good pic for my Starmax debut!

11:31.040 --> 11:32.170
Sorry, sorry.

11:32.170 --> 11:34.630
It's easier if you use the front cam.

11:34.630 --> 11:35.380
Where?

11:35.380 --> 11:38.260
Here. Want me to take one for you?

11:38.260 --> 11:39.340
Oh, sure.

11:39.340 --> 11:40.420
You hit this...

11:41.880 --> 11:42.900
See you.

11:42.900 --> 11:44.390
Bye-bye.

11:46.780 --> 11:49.580
I hope Kurume-san had fun.

11:49.580 --> 11:53.760
I'm sure she did. You put
people around you at ease.

11:53.760 --> 11:56.720
Aww, you really think so?

11:56.720 --> 11:59.140
I should send the Starmax pic to Fumi, too.

12:27.230 --> 12:30.470
My best sweater! Looks as cute as ever!

12:31.460 --> 12:33.890
Oops, I better deal with these pills.

12:34.680 --> 12:39.090
It's cool that Mitsu has at least
some interest in fashion.

12:39.090 --> 12:43.650
I even heard she and Fumi-chan went all
the way to Kanazawa to shop for clothes.

12:44.340 --> 12:48.610
From what I've seen,
she likes the bold, cutesy stuff.

12:48.610 --> 12:52.160
Like that bow-shaped purse and
those checkered pants, if I'm right.

12:52.160 --> 12:54.410
I'm off.

12:55.170 --> 12:57.420
Every one of them, all at once?!

12:57.420 --> 12:58.790
Wait, wait!

12:59.540 --> 13:01.410
Mitsu, do you still have time?!

13:01.410 --> 13:02.040
Yep.

13:02.040 --> 13:05.300
Please let me pick out your outfit!

13:05.300 --> 13:07.880
Today's an important day for you!

13:10.540 --> 13:11.680
A movie?

13:11.680 --> 13:13.680
Y-Yeah.

13:13.680 --> 13:16.740
You see, the one they're
showing until this weekend...

13:16.740 --> 13:19.480
Oh, that's our English reading assignment!

13:19.480 --> 13:21.490
It has a movie?

13:21.490 --> 13:23.490
Okay, one... two...

13:23.990 --> 13:26.240
D-Do you want to go see it together?

13:26.630 --> 13:28.490
What? Can we really?

13:30.430 --> 13:31.260
Yes!

13:31.260 --> 13:32.350
Mitsumi-chan.

13:32.350 --> 13:35.550
There's gonna be a class officer
meeting after school today.

13:35.550 --> 13:36.860
Where is it happening?

13:36.860 --> 13:38.720
In A/V Room B.

13:38.720 --> 13:40.380
Wait, isn't that...

13:40.730 --> 13:42.680
Oh, revival screenings?

13:42.680 --> 13:45.060
Where they bring back the superhits of old?

13:45.060 --> 13:46.480
Nice timing!

13:46.480 --> 13:49.010
It'll help with the assignment,
so count me in.

13:49.440 --> 13:51.640
What's everyone talking about?

13:57.760 --> 13:58.650
Okay.

14:00.940 --> 14:04.400
So this is the famous Hachiko statue.

14:04.840 --> 14:06.320
This is it, right?

14:06.320 --> 14:09.660
It's kinda hard to find for a meetup spot.

14:09.660 --> 14:10.740
There she is.

14:10.740 --> 14:11.660
Hey!

14:12.170 --> 14:14.910
Morning, Mitsumi-chan.

14:14.910 --> 14:17.910
Whoa, he's looking great!

14:17.910 --> 14:19.800
Sorry, did you wait long?

14:19.800 --> 14:23.280
Nah, I just got here. You're right on time.

14:23.930 --> 14:25.730
Feels like we're on a date, huh?

14:25.730 --> 14:28.680
Hey! We're here too!

14:29.010 --> 14:30.140
Good morning.

14:30.140 --> 14:31.650
Good morning, Kurume-san.

14:31.650 --> 14:35.290
I'm glad the weather's nice.
Thanks for inviting me.

14:36.930 --> 14:40.910
As I thought, these two are super plain!

14:41.570 --> 14:43.820
Huh? Why does that bag look so expensive?

14:45.190 --> 14:49.730
On the other hand, I read fashion mags
cover-to-cover before school began!

15:05.470 --> 15:09.080
I almost feel bad about how good
they're making me look.

15:09.080 --> 15:10.610
Shall we go?

15:10.610 --> 15:13.140
Oh, wait. I invited Yuzu-chan, too.

15:13.140 --> 15:13.930
Yu—

15:13.930 --> 15:15.060
Oh, there you are.

15:15.590 --> 15:16.870
Morning!

15:19.830 --> 15:20.760
Wha...

15:21.680 --> 15:24.310
Good job, Iwakura-san!

15:24.310 --> 15:26.180
Sorry, are we still good on time?

15:26.180 --> 15:27.980
We're grabbing a bite
before the movie, right?

15:27.980 --> 15:29.570
All good, all good!

15:31.100 --> 15:33.010
Bit early for lunch...

15:33.010 --> 15:35.030
I'm gonna go hard, though.

15:35.030 --> 15:38.390
Wow... I'm curious about this new dish.

15:38.390 --> 15:39.620
Dibs on him!

15:39.620 --> 15:41.580
Murashige-san, do you know
what you're getting?

15:41.580 --> 15:42.290
Yep.

15:42.290 --> 15:43.350
I'm set on the spicy chicken.

15:43.350 --> 15:45.520
Hot girls can make even
the simplest outfits look great.
I'm set on the spicy chicken.

15:45.520 --> 15:47.920
Hot girls can make even
the simplest outfits look great.

15:52.580 --> 15:55.260
They don't need to be all tryhard like me.

15:57.280 --> 15:58.430
Egashira-san.

15:58.430 --> 15:59.980
You're pretty stylish.

16:00.530 --> 16:02.680
Are you into fashion and stuff?

16:02.680 --> 16:03.570
Yeah...

16:03.570 --> 16:05.980
Right? You look like a model!

16:05.980 --> 16:08.530
Tell me where you buy your clothes!

16:08.530 --> 16:10.120
Thanks.

16:11.380 --> 16:14.040
I'm going with the Triple BBQ Steak!

16:14.040 --> 16:15.030
Talk about heavy.

16:15.030 --> 16:16.290
I've got room!

16:16.290 --> 16:18.750
He's a total mystery.

16:19.540 --> 16:21.910
Oh, the quiz the other day?

16:21.910 --> 16:24.290
That question was crazy!

16:24.290 --> 16:27.630
This app is great for learning vocab.

16:27.630 --> 16:30.420
Ooh, a study method from the future!

16:30.830 --> 16:33.800
I use it, too! Isn't it great?

16:35.310 --> 16:36.310
Yeah...

16:37.300 --> 16:39.100
Download finished!

16:39.930 --> 16:41.980
Then you do this...

16:43.350 --> 16:44.790
Yeah, like that.

16:44.790 --> 16:45.850
And then...

16:45.850 --> 16:47.720
Who ordered the tiramisu?

16:47.720 --> 16:48.480
Me.

16:51.260 --> 16:52.590
That looks great.

16:52.590 --> 16:53.790
Want a bite?

16:53.790 --> 16:57.530
Nah, I need to leave room for popcorn.

16:57.530 --> 17:02.180
I've always loved the caramel popcorn
at the movies, ever since I was little!

17:02.180 --> 17:04.540
Oh, I prefer salted.

17:04.540 --> 17:05.380
Caramel.

17:05.380 --> 17:06.510
Me too.

17:06.510 --> 17:07.560
Me three.

17:09.000 --> 17:10.460
I'm in Camp Salted.

17:11.900 --> 17:13.780
Yay! Salted buddies!

17:15.100 --> 17:16.940
I like salted, too.

17:22.270 --> 17:24.030
I'm so full, I might fall asleep!

17:24.030 --> 17:24.810
Idiot.

17:24.810 --> 17:26.550
Come on, man. You know how it is.

17:26.550 --> 17:27.810
Hey.
Come on, man. You know how it is.

17:27.810 --> 17:29.450
Aren't you sleepy?

17:29.450 --> 17:31.180
Sorry about all this.

17:32.200 --> 17:35.240
You only meant to invite Mitsumi, right?

17:37.530 --> 17:42.280
If you don't like people like me,
don't force yourself to talk to me.

17:42.760 --> 17:44.450
You can just chill out.

17:44.450 --> 17:46.680
No need to ruin your day off.

17:50.710 --> 17:51.960
I mean...

17:52.440 --> 17:54.210
Can you blame me?

17:54.720 --> 17:58.620
When I think about how people
probably find me a dweeb,

17:58.620 --> 18:00.630
I retreat into my shell.

18:00.630 --> 18:03.120
I just can't get all
buddy-buddy out of the blue.

18:04.440 --> 18:06.780
Yuzu-chan... Kurume-san...

18:08.120 --> 18:10.430
Wait, do they not get along?!

18:10.830 --> 18:11.920
Shoot!

18:11.920 --> 18:15.000
I invited her like I would have anyone
in my middle school class of eight,

18:15.000 --> 18:19.210
but with the increase in numbers, I should've
given more thought to compatibility!

18:19.210 --> 18:20.770
You guys grocery shopping too, Tacchan?

18:20.770 --> 18:22.620
I'm hitting the beach with Fumi
tomorrow. Wanna come?

18:22.620 --> 18:24.460
Sure, I'm in.

18:24.460 --> 18:26.700
I'm supposed to be the class officer!

18:26.700 --> 18:29.960
I better fix this!

18:30.420 --> 18:31.540
This should be good, huh?

18:31.540 --> 18:32.540
Yeah.

18:35.290 --> 18:37.710
I sat between them, but...

18:43.510 --> 18:45.150
Shima-kun!

18:51.150 --> 18:52.760
Want try some salted, too?

18:52.760 --> 18:55.400
Th-Thanks.

18:55.770 --> 18:58.910
I'm powerless.

19:09.420 --> 19:11.520
She's going to town on his popcorn!

19:13.320 --> 19:15.930
The alternating sweet and salty is yum!

19:15.930 --> 19:16.810
Really?

19:16.810 --> 19:18.040
Really, really!

19:18.040 --> 19:20.080
Can I share with Kurume-san
and Yuzu-chan, too?

19:20.080 --> 19:20.930
Go for it.

19:21.240 --> 19:21.980
Here.

19:22.420 --> 19:23.530
Thanks.

19:28.190 --> 19:29.420
Isn't it yummy?

19:29.420 --> 19:30.890
I guess...

19:33.640 --> 19:37.160
I think I'm joining Camp Caramel <i>and</i> Salted.

19:37.650 --> 19:39.890
Mitsumi-chan, can I try it too?

19:39.890 --> 19:41.170
Yeah, you should.

19:41.170 --> 19:42.780
It's really great!

19:44.860 --> 19:46.140
Thanks.

19:46.140 --> 19:47.150
Sure.

19:47.150 --> 19:48.950
Huh? What?

19:48.950 --> 19:50.940
What's up, Yuzu-chan?

19:51.580 --> 19:52.540
That's right.

19:53.670 --> 19:56.840
There was a side of me that
even found that drink tasty.

19:58.700 --> 20:02.200
Camp Caramel and Salted, huh?

20:07.830 --> 20:12.410
It's true that I don't like people
like you, but I want to change that.

20:12.410 --> 20:15.870
And I'd like to get to know
you better, Murashige-san.

20:37.840 --> 20:39.990
That was so good.

20:39.990 --> 20:41.840
It didn't feel outdated at all.

20:41.840 --> 20:43.950
Hey, what say we do some window shopping?

20:43.950 --> 20:45.340
Oh, I wanna!

20:45.340 --> 20:49.320
Let's get you some hair accessories.
They'd look great with your long hair.

20:49.320 --> 20:51.340
Huh? I-I'm good.

20:51.340 --> 20:53.980
What? But they'll suit you perfectly!

20:53.980 --> 20:57.800
Like a hair clip or something.
Simple, but it totally changes your vibe.

20:57.800 --> 20:58.210
No, I'm fine, really.

20:58.210 --> 20:59.480
They're buddy-buddy!
No, I'm fine, really.

21:00.650 --> 21:03.490
Guess I just misunderstood. Good, good.

21:04.560 --> 21:07.910
Mitsumi-chan, was this your
first time hanging out in Shibuya?

21:07.910 --> 21:08.980
Yep.

21:08.980 --> 21:12.340
Honestly, I used to think
it was this scary place.

21:12.340 --> 21:16.190
But walking around with you guys,
I get the appeal now.

21:17.390 --> 21:21.100
Yeah, it'd be nice if you came to like it.

21:21.100 --> 21:23.010
Shibuya, and Tokyo too.

21:23.010 --> 21:26.970
Yo, yo. Let's hit up Starmax after, yeah?

21:26.970 --> 21:31.010
He's just taken a liking
to Iwakura-san as a friend, right?

21:35.460 --> 21:39.520
I think memories of places are memories
of the people you went there with.

21:40.680 --> 21:41.680
Which is why...

22:04.230 --> 22:08.670
I'm sure I'll come to love this place!
